<article class="env-corollary" id="06MK">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06MK">Corollary <span data-tag="06MK">7.4.1.20</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a left fibration of $\infty $-categories and let $F: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a diagram which admits a limit. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The limit of $F$ is preserved by the covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
Every lift of $F$ to a diagram $\widetilde{F}: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ admits a limit which is preserved by the functor $U$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article>
